  ('ai:ai-batch-03:f58b4be281a5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Whose daughter was Elizabeth I?',array['Charles I''s','Henry VII''s','Henry VIII''s','James I''s']::text[],'C','''Elizabeth I, the daughter of Henry VIII''.',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Elizabeth I, the daughter of Henry VIII, became queen in 1558. She was popular with her people, partly because of the defeat of the Spanish Armada in 1588, a large fleet of ships sent by Spain to invade England. Her reign also saw a flowering of English drama, with playwrights such as William Shakespeare.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:24e064a5d885','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What was the Spanish Armada?',array['a royal wedding','a fleet of ships sent to invade England','a trade agreement','a Spanish army that captured London']::text[],'B','''A large fleet of ships sent by Spain to invade England.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Elizabeth I, the daughter of Henry VIII, became queen in 1558. She was popular with her people, partly because of the defeat of the Spanish Armada in 1588, a large fleet of ships sent by Spain to invade England. Her reign also saw a flowering of English drama, with playwrights such as William Shakespeare.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:d4ef2dae45cb','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Elizabeth I: which statement is supported by the text?',array['She was defeated by Spain.','English drama flourished during her reign.','She became queen in 1588.','She was unpopular with her people.']::text[],'B','''Her reign also saw a flowering of English drama.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Elizabeth I, the daughter of Henry VIII, became queen in 1558. She was popular with her people, partly because of the defeat of the Spanish Armada in 1588, a large fleet of ships sent by Spain to invade England. Her reign also saw a flowering of English drama, with playwrights such as William Shakespeare.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:398aa299c107','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Where did the Great Fire of London start?',array['on a ship','in a bakery','in Parliament','in a church']::text[],'B','''A fire broke out in a bakery in Pudding Lane.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','In 1666 a fire broke out in a bakery in Pudding Lane and spread across much of the City of London, destroying thousands of houses and many churches, including St Paul''s Cathedral. The architect Sir Christopher Wren was responsible for rebuilding St Paul''s, which still stands today.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:26c9300ec017','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Who rebuilt St Paul''s Cathedral?',array['Isaac Newton','Sir Christopher Wren','Isambard Kingdom Brunel','Henry VIII']::text[],'B','''Sir Christopher Wren was responsible for rebuilding St Paul''s.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','In 1666 a fire broke out in a bakery in Pudding Lane and spread across much of the City of London, destroying thousands of houses and many churches, including St Paul''s Cathedral. The architect Sir Christopher Wren was responsible for rebuilding St Paul''s, which still stands today.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:d915c1dda190','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What were members of the Women''s Social and Political Union called?',array['Cavaliers','Chartists','Roundheads','suffragettes']::text[],'D','''Its members became known as suffragettes.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','During the late 19th and early 20th centuries, women campaigned for the right to vote. In 1903 Emmeline Pankhurst founded the Women''s Social and Political Union, whose members became known as suffragettes. In 1918 women over the age of 30 were given the vote, and in 1928 women were given the vote at 21, the same age as men.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:d6494e5b226f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In which year did women get the vote on the same terms as men?',array['1945','1928','1903','1918']::text[],'B','''In 1928 women were given the vote at 21, the same age as men.''',array['life_in_uk','history','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','During the late 19th and early 20th centuries, women campaigned for the right to vote. In 1903 Emmeline Pankhurst founded the Women''s Social and Political Union, whose members became known as suffragettes. In 1918 women over the age of 30 were given the vote, and in 1928 women were given the vote at 21, the same age as men.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:3339e842e9f0','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which mountain range does the passage mention?',array['the Alps','the Pennines','the Himalayas','the Zagros']::text[],'D','''The foothills and ranges of the Zagros Mountains''.',array['kurdistan','world_knowledge','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','The Kurdistan Region of Iraq is mountainous, lying in the foothills and ranges of the Zagros Mountains. Rivers such as the Great Zab and the Little Zab flow south-west to join the Tigris. Lake Dukan, created by a dam on the Little Zab, is a popular place for visitors. Farmers in the valleys grow crops such as wheat, grapes and pomegranates.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:99ee9a83cdc5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How was Lake Dukan formed?',array['by melting ice','by an earthquake','by a volcano','by a dam on the Little Zab']::text[],'D','''Lake Dukan, created by a dam on the Little Zab''.',array['kurdistan','world_knowledge','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','The Kurdistan Region of Iraq is mountainous, lying in the foothills and ranges of the Zagros Mountains. Rivers such as the Great Zab and the Little Zab flow south-west to join the Tigris. Lake Dukan, created by a dam on the Little Zab, is a popular place for visitors. Farmers in the valleys grow crops such as wheat, grapes and pomegranates.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:f3521af7c57a','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which river do the Great and Little Zab join?',array['the Thames','the Euphrates','the Nile','the Tigris']::text[],'D','''Flow south-west to join the Tigris.''',array['kurdistan','world_knowledge','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','The Kurdistan Region of Iraq is mountainous, lying in the foothills and ranges of the Zagros Mountains. Rivers such as the Great Zab and the Little Zab flow south-west to join the Tigris. Lake Dukan, created by a dam on the Little Zab, is a popular place for visitors. Farmers in the valleys grow crops such as wheat, grapes and pomegranates.',null,null,null),
