  ('ai:ai-batch-03:fd9ea30d51c8','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The city of Sulaymaniyah was founded in ___ by the Baban prince Ibrahim Pasha.',array['1924','1484','1784','1884']::text[],'C','Sulaymaniyah was founded in 1784.',array['kurdistan','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:ea8ab38729d3','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which conclusion can be drawn from the timeline?',array['The Magna Carta was agreed in the 17th century.','The Great Fire happened before the Spanish Armada.','More than 600 years separate the Norman Conquest and the Act of Union.','The Act of Union and the Great Fire happened in the same century.']::text[],'C','1707 - 1066 = 641 years.',array['life_in_uk','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'image','samples/uk_timeline.png','Five dates in British history'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:23c070452302','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the chart. In which month is the temperature difference between Erbil and London greatest?',array['October','July','April','January']::text[],'B','July: 34 - 19 = 15 degrees, the largest gap.',array['kurdistan','life_in_uk','world_knowledge']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'video','samples/temperature_erbil_london.mp4','Erbil and London temperatures (8 seconds)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:703342ccce80','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which policy area remains reserved to Westminster?',array['defence','none of them','education','health']::text[],'A','''Defence and foreign affairs remain reserved.''',array['life_in_uk','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Since 1997 the UK has seen a significant devolution of power. The Scottish Parliament and the National Assembly for Wales (renamed the Senedd in 2020) were established in 1999, while the Northern Ireland Assembly emerged from the 1998 Good Friday Agreement. The devolved administrations legislate on areas such as health and education, whereas defence and foreign affairs remain reserved to the UK Parliament at Westminster.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:b9f394a68f05','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What was the National Assembly for Wales renamed in 2020?',array['the Senedd','the Dail','Holyrood','Stormont']::text[],'A','''Renamed the Senedd in 2020''.',array['life_in_uk','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Since 1997 the UK has seen a significant devolution of power. The Scottish Parliament and the National Assembly for Wales (renamed the Senedd in 2020) were established in 1999, while the Northern Ireland Assembly emerged from the 1998 Good Friday Agreement. The devolved administrations legislate on areas such as health and education, whereas defence and foreign affairs remain reserved to the UK Parliament at Westminster.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:fff1dfcab385','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What gave rise to the Northern Ireland Assembly?',array['the Good Friday Agreement','the Glorious Revolution','the Act of Union','the Magna Carta']::text[],'A','''Emerged from the 1998 Good Friday Agreement.''',array['life_in_uk','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Since 1997 the UK has seen a significant devolution of power. The Scottish Parliament and the National Assembly for Wales (renamed the Senedd in 2020) were established in 1999, while the Northern Ireland Assembly emerged from the 1998 Good Friday Agreement. The devolved administrations legislate on areas such as health and education, whereas defence and foreign affairs remain reserved to the UK Parliament at Westminster.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:63bd593a0cf7','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What point does the author make about ''first recorded'' uses?',array['They are always inaccurate.','They show that Shakespeare invented all of them.','They were added by later editors.','They do not prove that Shakespeare invented the expressions.']::text[],'D','''A first recorded use is not proof of invention.''',array['life_in_uk','culture','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Shakespeare''s influence on the English language is hard to overstate. Hundreds of words and phrases are first recorded in his plays and poems. Yet a first recorded use is not proof of invention: some expressions may simply reflect the everyday speech of his time, which happens to survive in his writing. Scholars therefore caution against crediting him with every phrase popularly attributed to him.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:1aee661faf44','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','The author''s attitude to popular claims about Shakespeare''s inventions is best described as ___.',array['cautious','indifferent','hostile','enthusiastic']::text[],'A','Scholars ''caution against crediting him with every phrase''.',array['life_in_uk','culture','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Shakespeare''s influence on the English language is hard to overstate. Hundreds of words and phrases are first recorded in his plays and poems. Yet a first recorded use is not proof of invention: some expressions may simply reflect the everyday speech of his time, which happens to survive in his writing. Scholars therefore caution against crediting him with every phrase popularly attributed to him.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:d41d1bcf7f48','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which script is used for Sorani?',array['a modified Arabic script','a Latin-based alphabet','the Cyrillic alphabet','no written form']::text[],'A','''Sorani... uses a modified Arabic script.''',array['kurdistan','culture','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Kurdish is not a single standardised language but a cluster of related varieties. Kurmanji, spoken by most Kurds in Turkey and Syria and in the Duhok area, is generally written in a Latin-based alphabet, whereas Sorani, prevalent in Erbil and Sulaymaniyah, uses a modified Arabic script. Speakers of the two varieties may find mutual comprehension challenging, particularly in writing.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:36345e55636c','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the passage, mutual comprehension between Kurmanji and Sorani speakers is ___.',array['always easy','completely impossible','identical in speech and writing','sometimes difficult, especially in writing']::text[],'D','''May find mutual comprehension challenging, particularly in writing.''',array['kurdistan','culture','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Kurdish is not a single standardised language but a cluster of related varieties. Kurmanji, spoken by most Kurds in Turkey and Syria and in the Duhok area, is generally written in a Latin-based alphabet, whereas Sorani, prevalent in Erbil and Sulaymaniyah, uses a modified Arabic script. Speakers of the two varieties may find mutual comprehension challenging, particularly in writing.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:422c56bc728a','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Where in the Kurdistan Region is Kurmanji spoken, according to the text?',array['only in Erbil','in the Duhok area','only in Sulaymaniyah','nowhere in the Region']::text[],'B','''And in the Duhok area''.',array['kurdistan','culture','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Kurdish is not a single standardised language but a cluster of related varieties. Kurmanji, spoken by most Kurds in Turkey and Syria and in the Duhok area, is generally written in a Latin-based alphabet, whereas Sorani, prevalent in Erbil and Sulaymaniyah, uses a modified Arabic script. Speakers of the two varieties may find mutual comprehension challenging, particularly in writing.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:1cabea5e0466','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What happens when peatland is drained?',array['It absorbs more carbon.','It releases the carbon it stores.','It turns into forest.','It stops decomposing.']::text[],'B','''Peat decomposes and releases this carbon.''',array['world_knowledge','nature','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Peatlands cover only around 3% of the Earth''s land surface, yet they are estimated to store more carbon than all the world''s forests combined. When drained for agriculture, peat decomposes and releases this carbon, turning a vital sink into a significant source of emissions. Restoration by re-wetting drained bogs is therefore increasingly seen as a cost-effective climate measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:520212a418f0','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In the passage on peatlands, a ''sink'' is ___.',array['a place where water drains away','something that absorbs and stores carbon','a type of farm','a source of emissions']::text[],'B','A carbon sink takes in and stores carbon.',array['world_knowledge','nature','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Peatlands cover only around 3% of the Earth''s land surface, yet they are estimated to store more carbon than all the world''s forests combined. When drained for agriculture, peat decomposes and releases this carbon, turning a vital sink into a significant source of emissions. Restoration by re-wetting drained bogs is therefore increasingly seen as a cost-effective climate measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:c46123cab822','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why is re-wetting bogs increasingly favoured?',array['It is required by law everywhere.','It is a cost-effective way to reduce emissions.','It creates new farmland.','It increases the area covered by forests.']::text[],'B','''Increasingly seen as a cost-effective climate measure.''',array['world_knowledge','nature','story']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03','Peatlands cover only around 3% of the Earth''s land surface, yet they are estimated to store more carbon than all the world''s forests combined. When drained for agriculture, peat decomposes and releases this carbon, turning a vital sink into a significant source of emissions. Restoration by re-wetting drained bogs is therefore increasingly seen as a cost-effective climate measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:dfe61add9fa8','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','To ''cross the Rubicon'' means to ___.',array['pass a point of no return','change sides repeatedly','travel abroad','avoid a difficult decision']::text[],'A','Julius Caesar crossed the river Rubicon in 49 BC, a step he could not undo.',array['world_knowledge','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:75569d422de9','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The Magna Carta is often cited as an early step towards the ___ of law.',array['throne','reign','crown','rule']::text[],'D','The ''rule of law'': no one is above the law.',array['life_in_uk','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:d0c8a05ff4b4','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which statement is best supported by the chart?',array['London''s summers are hotter than Erbil''s.','Both cities have the same temperature in October.','London is warmer than Erbil in January.','The seasonal range of temperature is much greater in Erbil than in London.']::text[],'D','Erbil ranges from about 7 to 34 degrees; London from about 5 to 19.',array['kurdistan','life_in_uk','world_knowledge']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'image','samples/temperature_erbil_london.png','Erbil and London temperatures (approximate)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:026f08bb6b58','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which pair of events on the timeline is separated by the shortest interval?',array['the Magna Carta and the Spanish Armada','the Spanish Armada and the Great Fire of London','the Great Fire of London and the Act of Union','the Norman Conquest and the Magna Carta']::text[],'C','1666 to 1707 is only 41 years.',array['life_in_uk','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'image','samples/uk_timeline.png','Five dates in British history'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:5eeb91fcf87c','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the timeline. Which event marks the creation of the Kingdom of Great Britain?',array['the Magna Carta','the Norman Conquest','the Act of Union','the Great Fire of London']::text[],'C','The Act of Union of 1707 united England and Scotland.',array['life_in_uk','history']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'video','samples/uk_timeline.mp4','Five dates in British history (10 seconds)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-03:10f67e2940dc','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the video. Approximately how much warmer is Erbil than London in July?',array['about 25 degrees','about 5 degrees','about 15 degrees','about 10 degrees']::text[],'C','34 - 19 = 15 degrees.',array['kurdistan','life_in_uk','world_knowledge']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-03',null,'video','samples/temperature_erbil_london.mp4','Erbil and London temperatures (8 seconds)')
